; ============================================================
; TITLE:    RGB Gradients
; CATEGORY: Generative Art & Colour
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     color, RGB, gradient, MAP, lists, interpolation
; SUMMARY:  Paints color gradients between any number of RGB colors, using MAP to blend lists.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A gradient is a smooth slide from one color to another. This
;   program blends two RGB lists with one MAP, then builds gradients
;   that pass through several color stops: a sunrise, an ocean, a
;   fire, a rainbow and a grey scale. Each is painted as a stack of
;   thin vertical lines with its name underneath.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Add your own gradient at the bottom with a name and a
;   list of colors.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * MAP with two lists at once: (MAP [...] :a :b)
;   * linear interpolation: a + t * (b - a)
;   * choosing which pair of color stops a point falls between
;   * ROUND to keep color values whole
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make a gradient with only two colors that are opposite on the
;     color wheel, like blue and orange. What appears in the middle?
;   * Paint the gradients in rings instead of bars.
;   * Add a gradient with 8 stops.
; ============================================================

; BLEND mixes two colors. :t = 0 gives :a and :t = 1 gives :b.
; MAP walks through both lists together: ?1 is from :a, ?2 from :b.
to blend :a :b :t
  output (map [round ?1 + :t * (?2 - ?1)] :a :b)
end

; COLOR.AT finds the color a fraction :t of the way along a list of
; stops. With 3 stops, 0 to 0.5 blends stops 1 and 2, and 0.5 to 1
; blends stops 2 and 3.
to color.at :stops :t
  localmake "gaps (count :stops) - 1
  localmake "where :t * :gaps
  localmake "k int :where
  ; The very last point sits exactly on the last stop.
  if :k >= :gaps [output last :stops]
  output blend item :k + 1 :stops item :k + 2 :stops :where - :k
end

; BAR paints a gradient 640 wide and 70 tall with its name below.
to bar :y :name :stops
  setpensize 2
  for [x 0 640 2] [
    setpencolor color.at :stops :x / 640
    penup setxy :x - 320 :y pendown
    setheading 0 forward 70
  ]
  setpencolor [70 70 70]
  penup setxy -320 :y - 18 pendown
  label :name
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [250 250 250]
setlabelheight 14
bar 190 "sunrise [[40 30 90] [230 80 90] [255 200 90]]
bar 85 "ocean [[0 30 60] [0 120 160] [120 220 220] [240 250 240]]
bar -20 "fire [[30 0 0] [200 30 0] [255 150 0] [255 255 180]]
bar -125 "rainbow [[255 0 0] [255 160 0] [255 255 0] [0 200 0] [0 120 255] [130 0 200]]
bar -230 "greys [[0 0 0] [255 255 255]]
